From fb16560054b44899c50b8aec5ce1a2b0e35c0533 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:36:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: report done after queueing the out-of-light stair
 command

borg_think_dungeon_light()'s staircase branch queued '<' but fell
through without returning, so the routine reported "nothing done"
while a stair command was already queued -- and the caller's think loop
kept queueing more commands behind it, all of which would land on the
new level after the stairs were taken. Return true.
---
 src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
index a0255e4be..559d06053 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
@@ -192,6 +192,9 @@ bool borg_think_dungeon_light(void)
                 borg_note("# Testing for stairs .");
 
                 borg_keypress('<');
+
+                /* Done */
+                return true;
             }
         }
 
-- 
2.53.0

